    "text.286f757d": "If ‘young’ (少) is a quality still growing and unfolding, ‘old’ (老) is one that has fully ripened and reached a turning point. iYeok reads the change of old yin and old yang as a quality that deepens until the possibility of moving toward another quality opens up. Neither is better or higher than the other.",
