    "text.b533adf4": null,
    "text.b56f1013": null,
    "text.b70e6471": null,
    "text.b7297483": "In the yarrow method read by few and many (少·多), too, when one of the three rounds differs, that one decides whether the line is yin or yang; when all three are the same, the line becomes a changing line. Rather than a simple majority vote, iYeok also reads this as a question: “In this combination, which quality is given the deciding voice?”",
    "text.b75221e8": null,
    "text.b7748ee4": null,
    "text.b797a193": null,
    "text.b79e5570": null,
    "text.b82b82d4": "We cannot choose the conditions we are born into, but there is no need to dislike the self we were born as. Nor do we need to confine ourselves to who we are now. What to accept and which direction to live in is ours to consider and choose. This is also why iYeok lets you choose among different methods.",
    "text.b84d6a7b": null,
    "text.b85a8a31": "Back to start",
